  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A circuit is arranged as shown in figure. The output voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></math> is equal to __________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0110_63bbf9cae37c.png\" style=\"width: 343px; height: 196px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0110_7897132625e5.png\" style=\"width: 342px; height: 193px;\" /></p><p>Diodes are forward biased, so they act as wire so input current is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;as input source is short circuited output current is also zero, as input current is zero</p><p>Now, output voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>"
  }
